@tradition farewell-supper
// Farewell supper (seasons designer, k 483; baked since 0.34.43). The day before each crew rotation (rotation days are
// Sundays, so a Saturday): when: rotation -1; its honorees are that rotation's leavers ({names}, {first}); the word
// friends-of-honoree is affinity 40 or more with any leaver. Design note: plans/trad-notes-seasons.md.
k: 483
title: Farewell supper
when: rotation -1
at: 18:00-19:20
min: 30
prio: 2
jitter: 10
early: 5
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
where: 3 pool mess-seat
hold: 1
who: honoree always, friends-of-honoree 85%, everyone 15%
anim: talk
from: brennan
ties: galley meal=dinner dish=favourite
ties: decor longTables

== mail
- Sunday's shuttle takes {names} away from the Wren. Farewell supper tomorrow, {time}, in the mess. Come and say goodbye properly.

== ask
- Farewell supper for {first} tonight. I'm not ready.   #warm
- Supper for {first} at six. Sit with us?
- I've written {first} a card. It's mostly jokes. Some of it isn't.   #warm

== here
- To {names}. The Wren won't be the same.   #warm
- Remember the night the lift stuck? {first} sang the whole time.   #funny
- Write to us. Properly, not just one line.   #warm
- Save a seat for {first}. It's still theirs tonight.

== thanks
- You join the long table for the farewell supper for {names}. There's laughing, and one or two quiet bits.   #warm

== chatter
- I'll miss {first}. The new posting sounds good, though.
- The farewell supper always goes on later than anyone plans.   #warm
